## Knowledge search (ksearch) — installed

```bash
python3 scripts/ksearch.py "<query>"          # ranked excerpts + file pointers (~500 tokens, not whole files)
python3 scripts/ksearch.py "<query>" --dir rules   # narrow to a subdir
python3 scripts/ksearch.py "<query>" --json   # machine-readable
```

Stdlib-only; reads `knowledge/` (override with `KB_ROOT`). Every query is logged to `knowledge/_ksearch-log.tsv` for the zero-hit audit ([hygiene.md](../rules/hygiene.md)).

## Code structure (ripgrep / ripwire) — recommended

```bash
rg "<literal>"                       # string literals, configs, non-code files
ripwire <dir> --for="<task>"         # ranked signatures for a task (if installed)
ripwire <dir> --callers=<SYM>        # who calls SYM
ripwire <dir> --impact=<SYM>         # transitive blast radius
```

Prefer ripwire over grep for who-calls-what, blast radius, structural discovery, reuse hotspots. Fall back to `rg` for literals and non-code files.

## Skills

Two skill procedures ship with the KB — canonical content in [skills/](skills/README.md), thin per-harness stubs in `.agents/skills/`:

- **distill** — the bootstrap distillation pass (SCAFFOLDED → VERIFIED). Invoked via the stub, or by following [skills/distill.md](skills/distill.md) directly.
- **kb-audit** — the consolidation pass (query-log review, label spot-check, reference audit).

## Knowledge gate (pre-commit)

`scripts/knowledge-gate.py` validates staged knowledge changes (TL;DR-at-birth, links, plan Status, anti-truncation, KB status-line rules). Wiring snippet: `.pre-commit-knowledge-gate-snippet.yaml` at repo root after `kbase-init`.
